{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Also</b>, he says, <b>to those who rebuke, lips</b> — [verses 23–26] four joined. <b>These things too</b> are known to the wise — they are the masters of justice, for showing partiality in judgment is not good. And the judge who says to the wicked in his case, 'You are righteous' — let the peoples curse him, because he did not do justice according to justice." "<b>To those who rebuke</b> — the wicked for their wickedness — the pleasantness of YHWH will come to them."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:32.119235913Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}